        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 84-year-old male patient, admitted on 02/01/2014 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, clinical examination revealed reduced air entry bilaterally with expiratory wheeze and increased work of breathing. Oxygen saturation was diminished at room air. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation without consolidation. Blood tests demonstrated a mild inflammatory response. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and intravenous fluids. Clinical response was satisfactory with improvement of symptoms and oxygen saturation. He was discharged on 03/01/2014 in stable condition. Please continue maintenance bronchodilator therapy and ensure close outpatient follow-up. Smoking cessation and pulmonary rehabilitation referral are recommended.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
